[
 {
  "section": "Parts page & queue",
  "key": "SA-20b",
  "title": "Answering \u201cIn stock? Yes\u201d while pricing already reads as \u201cIn stock\u201d",
  "sub": "The 8/30 run stopped the approval-time pre-fill; the same Yes \u2192 \u201cIn stock\u201d / No \u2192 \u201cOn order\u201d rule still fires the moment the answer is given while pricing.",
  "dims": [
   "UX Med",
   "Size S",
   "Codex 0\u20131",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: every parts user pricing a part before the estimate goes out \u2014 every multi-person shop"
  ],
  "pop": "The parts counter \u2014 a part reads \u201cOn order\u201d before the customer has even seen the estimate, and before anyone ordered anything.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>What the part reads while pricing</span><span class=\"hint\">scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"scroller\">\n          <table class=\"plain\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr><th scope=\"col\">Answer while pricing</th><th scope=\"col\">Today the part reads</th><th scope=\"col\">Proposed</th></tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">Yes</td>\n                <td>In stock</td>\n                <td>Pending &mdash; the Yes stays shown as the answer it is</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">No</td>\n                <td>On order</td>\n                <td>Pending</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"surface-name\">? &mdash; not answered</td>\n                <td>Pending</td>\n                <td>Pending</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"viz-foot\">Delivery state is set only when a parts user actually does the thing &mdash; pulls it, or orders it.</div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Plain \u201cPending\u201d at pricing time, or hide the delivery cell until the line is approved? rec: Pending"
   ],
   [
    "check",
    "The parts queue and the approval roll-ups read this state \u2014 the build confirms an un-filled \u201cPending\u201d doesn\u2019t move an RO in or out of the queue differently."
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": [
   "Extend the 8/30 ruling \u2014 the Yes / No / ? answer stays displayed as the answer it is; delivery state is set only when a parts user actually does the thing. Dave, 31 Aug"
  ]
 },
 {
  "section": "Parts page & queue",
  "key": "Q",
  "title": "Parts RO page: the labor line card is too tall (one line + 2 parts \u2248 830 px)",
  "sub": "On the parts user\u2019s RO page a single line with two parts fills most of the screen; the counter scrolls constantly.",
  "dims": [
   "UX Med",
   "Size M (mockup round first)",
   "Codex 0\u20131 (visual only)",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: every parts user, every RO"
  ],
  "pop": "The parts counter working a multi-line RO on the dark parts page.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>Today&rsquo;s card, on the parts page</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"screens\">\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"as-darkscreen\">\n              <div class=\"dk-head\">\n                <span class=\"dk-ro\">RO #</span>\n                <span class=\"dk-veh\">Year Make Model</span>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"dk-body\">\n                <div class=\"as-darkcard\">\n                  <div class=\"dc-title\">Line title</div>\n                  <div>\n                    <div class=\"dc-band\">Complaint</div>\n                    <div class=\"dc-text\"><span style=\"display:block;height:7px;border-radius:4px;background:#334155;width:96%;margin:4px 0\"></span><span style=\"display:block;height:7px;border-radius:4px;background:#334155;width:88%;margin:4px 0\"></span></div>\n                  </div>\n                  <div>\n                    <div class=\"dc-band\">Cause</div>\n                    <div class=\"dc-text\"><span style=\"display:block;height:7px;border-radius:4px;background:#334155;width:94%;margin:4px 0\"></span><span style=\"display:block;height:7px;border-radius:4px;background:#334155;width:70%;margin:4px 0\"></span></div>\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"dc-band\">Parts needed</div>\n                  <div class=\"dc-part\"><span class=\"pn\">Part #</span><b>Part 1</b></div>\n                  <div class=\"dc-part\"><span class=\"pn\">Part #</span><b>Part 2</b></div>\n                  <div class=\"dc-foot\"><span>Labor hours</span><b>Line total</b></div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"dk-measure\">\n                <svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 3v18M8 6l4-3 4 3M8 18l4 3 4-3\"/></svg>\n                one line + 2 parts &asymp; 830 px\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>Today</b> &mdash; one line fills most of the screen.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </figure>",
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>Three ways to get it shorter</span><span class=\"hint\">scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"scroller\">\n          <div class=\"sils\">\n            <div class=\"sil-col\">\n              <span class=\"sil-h now\">&asymp; 830 px</span>\n              <div class=\"sil now\" style=\"height:150px;\"></div>\n              <span class=\"sil-lbl\">Today</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"sil-col\">\n              <span class=\"sil-h\">shorter</span>\n              <div class=\"sil\" style=\"height:112px;\"></div>\n              <span class=\"sil-lbl\">Tighter padding</span>\n              <span class=\"sil-tbd\">px saved: TBD</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"sil-col\">\n              <span class=\"sil-h\">shorter</span>\n              <div class=\"sil\" style=\"height:96px;\"></div>\n              <span class=\"sil-lbl\">Complaint/Cause 1 line each</span>\n              <span class=\"sil-tbd\">px saved: TBD</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"sil-col\">\n              <span class=\"sil-h\">shorter</span>\n              <div class=\"sil\" style=\"height:84px;\"></div>\n              <span class=\"sil-lbl\">&ldquo;Parts Needed&rdquo; rail turned sideways</span>\n              <span class=\"sil-tbd\">px saved: TBD</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"viz-foot\">Mockups with a real RO next, if this advances. Re-opens the 8/21 two-line Complaint/Cause rule on purpose.</div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Which variants go on the ballot \u2014 your 3 + which extras (collapse the notes band, part on one row, one-line footer, per-user density)?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Complaint/Cause: 1 line + hover, or keep 2 and shrink elsewhere?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Sideways \u201cParts Needed\u201d rail worth the legibility cost?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Parts page only, or advisor/tech cards too?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Target height for one line + 2 parts?"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
  "section": "RO page \u2014 advisor, admin, tech",
  "key": "P",
  "title": "Admin RO page: the Parts & Labor card hides the parts the counter already added",
  "sub": "Locked, an admin sees \u201cAdd a part\u2026\u201d, \u201cParts subtotal \u2014\u201d, \u201cPricing to follow\u201d \u2014 while the parts counter\u2019s view of the same line shows RC-FP-002 \u00b7 Fuel pump module (recall) \u00b7 stock ? \u00b7 unpriced.",
  "dims": [
   "UX High",
   "Size M",
   "Codex 2\u20133 (touches who-may-edit and the checkout hold)",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: every admin opening an RO with parts on it"
  ],
  "pop": "Admins reviewing an RO before it goes to the customer \u2014 they can\u2019t see what parts has done.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>Same line, two minutes apart</span><span class=\"hint\">screens scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"screens\">\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-body\">\n                <div class=\"as-panel\">\n                  <div class=\"as-panel-lbl\">Parts view</div>\n                  <div class=\"as-linelist\">\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\"><b>RC-FP-002</b> &middot; Fuel pump module (recall)</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\">In stock?</span><span class=\"tail\">?</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\">Note</span><span class=\"tail\" style=\"font-style:italic\">the counter&rsquo;s note</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\">Qty</span><span class=\"tail\">1</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\">Unit price</span><span class=\"tail\">unpriced</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow count\"><span class=\"grow\">Parts total</span><span class=\"tail\">Sum / Manual</span></div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>What parts sees</b> &mdash; the part is on the line, named and noted.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-body\">\n                <div class=\"as-panel\">\n                  <div class=\"as-panel-lbl\">Admin, locked</div>\n                  <div class=\"as-linelist\">\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"mark\">+</span><span class=\"grow\" style=\"color:#94a3b8;\">Add a part&hellip;</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\">Parts subtotal</span><span class=\"tail\">&mdash;</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"as-lrow\"><span class=\"grow\" style=\"color:#94a3b8;\">Pricing to follow</span></div>\n                  </div>\n                  <span class=\"as-tag\" style=\"margin-top:8px;\">\n                    <svg width=\"9\" height=\"9\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12\"/></svg>\n                    the part is invisible here\n                  </span>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>What the admin sees</b> &mdash; an empty row where the fuel pump is.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"viz-foot\"><b>Proposed:</b> locked = the full parts picture, read-only; &ldquo;Edit pricing&rdquo; unlocks all of it &mdash; the way the labor rate already works on this card.</div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Locked view = the parts page\u2019s row exactly, or the money ledger\u2019s row with stock + note added?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Edit mode gets the Note cell and the Sum/Manual parts total too?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Admin gets the \u26a0 unpriced flag and \u00d7 delete per row?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "If a parts user is mid-edit on the line \u2014 take over with the warning, or refuse?"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
  "section": "RO page \u2014 advisor, admin, tech",
  "key": "SA-6b",
  "title": "A line the close auto-declined reads \u201cDeclined by the customer\u201d",
  "sub": "Closing an RO now settles every unanswered line as declined \u2014 the 8/30 rule \u2014 and the line\u2019s banner then borrows the customer\u2019s name for it.",
  "dims": [
   "UX Med",
   "Size S",
   "Codex 0\u20131",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: any RO closed while a line still had no customer answer \u2014 read later by the advisor, or in an audit"
  ],
  "pop": "Whoever opens the closed RO and reads that the customer said no, when the customer never answered.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>What happens today, step by step</span></figcaption>\n        <ol class=\"story\">\n          <li>\n            <span class=\"stephead\">\n              <span class=\"n\">1</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2.6 12s3.5-6.4 9.4-6.4S21.4 12 21.4 12s-3.5 6.4-9.4 6.4S2.6 12 2.6 12z\"/><path d=\"M4 20 20 4\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>The customer <b>never answers</b> on one line.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li>\n            <span class=\"stephead\">\n              <span class=\"n\">2</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M8.4 12.3l2.4 2.4 4.8-5\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>The advisor <b>closes the RO</b>.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li>\n            <span class=\"stephead\">\n              <span class=\"n\">3</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3.5 6h17M3.5 12h17M3.5 18h9\"/><path d=\"M15.5 15.5 21 21M21 15.5 15.5 21\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>That line is <b>settled as declined</b> at close.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li class=\"bad\">\n            <span class=\"stephead\">\n              <span class=\"n\">4</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 3 2.5 20h19L12 3z\"/><path d=\"M12 9.5v4.5M12 17h.01\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>Its banner reads <b>&ldquo;Declined by the customer&rdquo;</b> &mdash; the customer never said no.</p>\n          </li>\n        </ol>\n        <div class=\"viz-foot\">That wording appears on exactly one surface today: the line&rsquo;s banner on the RO page. The customer&rsquo;s own page never shows it, and dashboards and money bands count the line as declined without naming who. The RO already carries a &ldquo;closed without a response&rdquo; mark the label can be read from.</div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Label it \u201cDeclined at close\u201d, read from the RO\u2019s own closed-without-a-response mark? rec: yes"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Dashboards and money bands keep counting it as declined \u2014 only the banner names the reason? rec: yes"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
  "section": "RO page \u2014 advisor, admin, tech",
  "key": "W",
  "title": "\u201cSend to advisor\u201d warns about the customer seeing a gap on lines the customer can\u2019t see",
  "sub": "On a recon-only RO the warning says a customer will see an unpriced part \u2014 there is no customer.",
  "dims": [
   "Reliability Low",
   "Size S",
   "Codex 0\u20131",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: recon stores sending to the advisor"
  ],
  "pop": "Anyone at a recon store sending an RO to the advisor \u2014 the warning is always wrong there.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>The message &mdash; today vs proposed</span><span class=\"hint\">screens scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"screens\">\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-body\">\n                <div class=\"as-toast bad\">\n                  <svg width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"flex:none; color:#dc2626;\"><path d=\"M12 3 2.5 20h19L12 3z\"/><path d=\"M12 9.5v4.5M12 17h.01\"/></svg>\n                  <span>The customer will see <b>2 lines with an unpriced part</b>.</span>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>Today</b> &mdash; on a recon RO there is no customer to see anything.</p>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-body\">\n                <div class=\"as-toast ok\">\n                  <svg width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"flex:none; color:#059669;\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M12 8v4.5M12 16h.01\"/></svg>\n                  <span><b>2 recon lines still have a blank price</b>.</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"as-btn none\">&mdash; or no message at all</div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>Proposed</b> &mdash; internal wording, or nothing.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Leave internal lines out entirely, or keep them with internal wording?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Same for warranty/recall (customer sees them at $0)?"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
  "section": "RO page \u2014 advisor, admin, tech",
  "key": "S",
  "title": "A tech can re-open labor hours after the estimate went out (park \u2192 un-park)",
  "sub": "Hours lock once the RO leaves the tech\u2019s stages \u2014 but parking the RO in Holding and un-parking it lands back in In service, where hours are editable again, under an estimate the customer already has.",
  "dims": [
   "Reliability Med",
   "Size M",
   "Codex 2\u20133 (permission rule \u2014 client + server together)",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: stores with a Holding status; no report of it happening"
  ],
  "pop": "Nobody yet \u2014 but it moves a total under an estimate the customer is holding.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>The two-step way around the lock</span></figcaption>\n        <ol class=\"story\">\n          <li>\n            <span class=\"stephead\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M14 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z\"/><path d=\"M14 3v5h5\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>The RO is <b>awaiting the customer</b> &mdash; hours are locked.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li>\n            <span class=\"stephead\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" rx=\"3\"/><path d=\"M9.5 9.5v5M14.5 9.5v5\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>The tech <b>parks</b> it in Holding, then <b>un-parks</b> it.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li class=\"bad\">\n            <span class=\"stephead\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"/><path d=\"M12 7.5V12l3 1.6\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>It lands in <b>Ready for Pickup</b>, where hours are editable again.</p>\n          </li>\n          <li class=\"bad\">\n            <span class=\"stephead\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>\n              <svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.9\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M12 2.5v19\"/><path d=\"M17 6.5H9.8a3.3 3.3 0 0 0 0 6.6h4.4a3.3 3.3 0 0 1 0 6.6H6.5\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n            <p>The tech <b>adds 2 hours</b> &mdash; the line total moves under a sent estimate.</p>\n          </li>\n        </ol>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "",
    "Is the rule \u201cno tech hour edits after the estimate is sent\u201d (one-way fact) or \u201conly in these stages\u201d?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "If estimate-based: does un-parking legitimately re-open hours for a real re-diagnosis \u2014 and who re-sends?"
   ],
   [
    "",
    "Same rule for the advisor/admin ledger, which has no stage lock today?"
   ]
  ],
  "ruled": []
 },
 {
  "section": "Dashboards",
  "key": "D3",
  "title": "Admin dashboard: the Pipeline / List switch gets squashed to \u201cLi\u201d when a filter is on",
  "sub": "Turn on any filter and the toolbar runs out of room \u2014 \u201cList\u201d becomes \u201cLi\u201d.",
  "dims": [
   "UX Med",
   "Size S",
   "Codex 0\u20131",
   "Reversible: code only",
   "Population: every admin, every filtered view"
  ],
  "pop": "Any admin who filters the dashboard \u2014 that\u2019s most sessions.",
  "styles": [],
  "blocks": [
   "<figure class=\"viz\">\n        <figcaption class=\"viz-cap\"><span>The toolbar &mdash; today vs fixed</span><span class=\"hint\">screens scroll &rarr;</span></figcaption>\n        <div class=\"screens\">\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-scroll\">\n                <div class=\"as-toolbar tight\">\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl grow\">Search&hellip;</span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">All statuses <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">Derek Jozwiak <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">Technician <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl clear\">&times; Clear</span>\n                  <span class=\"as-seg\"><span class=\"on\">Pipeline</span><span class=\"as-cut\">Li</span></span>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>Today</b> &mdash; the switch is the thing that gives, so the word breaks in half.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"screen-col\">\n            <div class=\"app-screen\">\n              <div class=\"as-scroll\">\n                <div class=\"as-toolbar tight\">\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl grow squash\">Search&hellip;</span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">All statuses <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">Derek Jozwiak <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl\">Technician <svg width=\"8\" height=\"8\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m6 9 6 6 6-6\"/></svg></span>\n                  <span class=\"as-ctl clear\">&times; Clear</span>\n                  <span class=\"as-seg\"><span class=\"on\">Pipeline</span><span>List</span></span>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"scap\"><b>Fixed</b> &mdash; the switch keeps both words whole; the search box gives instead.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </figure>"
  ],
  "questions": [
   [
    "check",
    "Ship as a plain fix \u2014 no design decision? rec: yes"
   ]
